  "notes": "{齧|かじ}る is a transitive godan verb with both a physical and figurative meaning.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n\nLITERAL SENSE:\nTo bite or gnaw at something with the front teeth. Used for animals gnawing and for biting into hard foods.\n- 〜を{齧|かじ}る: to nibble/gnaw on ~\n- {爪|つめ}を{齧|かじ}る: to bite one's nails\n\nFIGURATIVE SENSE:\nTo have only superficial knowledge; to dabble. Often self-deprecating.\n- {哲学|てつがく}を{齧|かじ}った{程度|ていど}: just dabbled in philosophy\n- {少|すこ}し{齧|かじ}ったことがある: to have dabbled a bit in ~\n\nWRITING:\nThe kanji {齧|かじ} is complex and often written in hiragana (かじる), especially in casual contexts.",
